<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="distribution" data-rev="1">
  <!-- @include-skip hand-written rows mirror 04-plan-distribution.yaml; same structure as the sibling plan fragments -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">config</span> .cargo/config.toml</summary><div class="pl-card">Static C runtime for the Windows target; the current release binary imports VCRUNTIME140.dll, which a clean machine lacks.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>build</td><td>+6</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-mod"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> cli.rs, launch.rs, web.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The launcher finds the page folder beside the binary, chooses and prints a seed when none is given, and opens the default browser with --open. No new command.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>cli</td><td>+79 / -5</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> install_layout.rs, release_version.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The installed layout runs from an unrelated folder with no configuration; the version string, the hello message, and the workspace version are one value.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>cli tests</td><td>+220</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">infra</span> packaging/windows/installer.nsi, build.ps1</summary><div class="pl-card">Per-user NSIS installer with a Start-menu entry and uninstaller; the build names the setup file from the binary's own version.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>packaging</td><td>+190</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">infra</span> packaging/windows/smoke.ps1, run-sandbox.ps1</summary><div class="pl-card">A clean Windows 11 sandbox installs silently, starts the shortcut, waits for kick-off, screenshots the page, checks the version, and uninstalls.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>packaging</td><td>+210</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-mod"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> packaging/README.md, README.md, .gitignore</summary><div class="pl-card">How to build, install, and smoke-test; the unsigned-download warning; dist/ ignored.</div></details></td><td>new + modified</td><td>root</td><td>+73</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="callout callout-danger pl-risk"><strong>Awaiting the product owner.</strong> Which operating systems ship beyond Windows, and how an installed user starts a match. The Windows steps do not change with either answer.</div>
  <div class="callout callout-warn pl-risk"><strong>Clean-machine runtime.</strong> The release binary needs the Visual C++ runtime today; step 1 links it statically and the sandbox run proves it.</div>
  <div class="callout callout-warn pl-risk"><strong>Unsigned download.</strong> SmartScreen warns on a downloaded setup file; the sandbox copy does not reproduce the warning.</div>
  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>Prior revisions</summary><p>Revision 0 (2026-09-22): first plan, stopped on two product questions. Snapshot: <a href="history/04-plan-distribution-0.md">history/04-plan-distribution-0.md</a>.</p><p>Revision 1 (2026-09-23): auto-review. Page-folder discovery now matches content discovery, and stale citations are refreshed. Both questions remain open.</p></details>
